# Cliffhangers. A `hook` is the last line of its flight day; its resolver (`due`,
# `when fired <hook>`) opens the next day. The engine spaces hooks >= 4 days apart.
# Resolutions: mostly satisfying, sometimes ominous, never "it was nothing".
# All hooks share hook_who to carry the astronaut over; they never overlap.
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

# --- 1. The missed knock (late clock) -------------------------------------------
card h_band
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 30 34
weight 24
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 23:40. The old-channel carrier on {A}'s dish misses a knock, the first miss in weeks. {A} watches the clock run past eleven seconds, then twelve, then thirty.

# --- 2. Cabin pressure -------------------------------------------------------
card h_pressure
type event
cat repair
hook
once
days 4 27
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 01:50. The cabin pressure on {A}'s ship is falling, a tenth of a kilopascal an hour. {A} is the only one awake.

# --- 3. Solar flare ----------------------------------------------------------
card h_flare
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 7 33
weight 9
roles A
when cond A ok
when !fired storm_shelter
do who hook_who A
text 23:52. The space weather feed flags a major flare on the Sun. Its protons will reach the fleet in about forty minutes. {A} starts calling the other ships.

# --- 4. Uncommanded thruster --------------------------------------------------
card h_thruster
type event
cat repair skill
hook
once
days 4 27
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 02:14. {A}'s ship starts to roll with nothing in the command log. The control loop fires a thruster to stop it. Then another. {A} is already at the console.

card valve_later
type event
cat repair
due
once
days 24 33
roles A
when flag valve_out
when is A valve_who
when since t_valve >= 6
text Every attitude move on {A}'s ship now takes a beat longer, routed around the valve that was isolated that night. The flight software has a new line in it with {A}'s initials. {A} has stopped noticing, mostly, except at 02:00.
do morale A -1

# --- 5. Alarm flood -----------------------------------------------------------
card h_flood
type event
cat repair skill
hook
once
days 4 27
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Just before midnight, 214 alarms hit {A}'s console at once. One of them is real.

# --- 6. Ground silence --------------------------------------------------------
card h_silence
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 10 27
weight 8
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Mission Control misses a scheduled check-in. Then the next one. {A} sends a third hail and starts the clock: twice the light time, plus a minute for someone to put a coffee down.

# --- 7. Hull strike -----------------------------------------------------------
card h_strike
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 4 27
weight 9
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Something hits {A}'s ship hard enough to tick through the whole hull. Every pressure reading is green. {A} doesn't trust green.

# --- 8. Star tracker ghost (ominous) ---------------------------------------------
card h_ghost
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 33
weight 14
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 02:10. {A}'s star tracker drops out of lock: one star too many in the field, and the next frame doesn't agree with the first. Attitude hands over to the backup tracker, which has never been asked to fly alone.

# --- 9. A voice on the loop ----------------------------------------------------------
card h_voice
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 33
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 02:40. The intercom on {A}'s ship opens and plays four seconds of a kitchen somewhere: a kettle, a radio, someone laughing. Nothing in the comms log says a call came in.

# --- 10. A ship drops off the net -------------------------------------------------
card h_dark
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 26 29
weight 14
roles A
when cond A ok
when since t_frame >= 1
do who hook_who A
text 23:58. {A}'s ship stops answering on the fleet net in the middle of a sentence. No telemetry, just an empty slot on six displays. Through the next ship's long lens, its cabin windows are lit as usual.

